    "details": {
      "alignment": "Neutral",
      "type": {
        "value": "humanoid",
        "subtype": "Toad"
      },
      "cr": 0.5,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — John Lee.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, generated from the article's own words. no XP ledger entry; archetype default → CR 1/2 as a soldier. Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Ceremonial Guard Who Got Lost in the Right Direction</strong> — Peach's Castle — ceremonial guard of the palace (955 BF); father of Toad Lee</p><p>Status: Unknown as of 1040 BF — last on the record at dawn in Efferd, 955 BF, in Fawful's Bean Badge, asking the Mages' Guild for an escort to his son; no later account places him anywhere</p><p>A ceremonial guard at Peach's Castle in the last month of the reign: a Toad whose job was to stand next to a lantern and look like the kingdom was fine. On one night in Efferd, 955 BF he jumped four times because the Mario brothers were coming, got lost five times in the right direction, and ended up in the dungeon corridor where a Koopa who was never locked in shook Fawful's hand with the Mages' Guild watching. He is the only witness the archive has to the Arrangement with a voice, and the first man the Chamberlain told the Guild to kill. He left the castle through the drains with a dead Toad's shortsword, a letter that was not addressed to him and the captain's sash on both arms. His son is the Disaster Inc. Toad Lee.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Sabre</strong> — “He left the castle through the drains with a dead Toad's shortsword, a letter that was not addressed to him and the captain's sash on both arms.”</li><li><strong>Sneak Attack</strong> — “A second ambush out of a pipe.”</li><li><strong>Pack Tactics</strong> — “On one night in Efferd, 955 BF he jumped four times because the Mario brothers were coming, got lost five times in the right direction, and ended up in the dungeon corridor where a Koopa who was never locked in shook”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/john_lee</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/john_lee</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
    },
